<!--
  CHILL_HEATED_SUIT_1 — the heated dive suit, one clock (a battery charge
  gauge; card ruling declined both the two-clock heat+air option and the
  no-clock option). Full mechanism, Odyssey-research writeup and the
  hypothermia-math this leans on: RM_CompHeatedSuitBattery.cs's own header.

  ParentName="Apparel_Vacsuit" DELIBERATELY — Odyssey already ships exactly
  "the appropriate suit type" (Defs/Odyssey/ThingDefs_Misc/Apparel_Various.
  xml, MEASURED via RimSage this session): real shipped art, armor,
  insulation, EquipDelay, body coverage, even the "restricts movement"
  framing, all for free. This def inherits that whole shape and only
  overrides what the Chill's own ruling actually asks for: Insulation_Cold
  cut from the inherited 90 down to a modest 20 (see the .cs header — the
  full -110C counteraction is charge-gated via RM_StatPart_HeatedSuitCharge,
  not a static apparel stat, or an empty suit would still be halfway safe)
  and the battery comp itself.

  ART: reuses Odyssey's real Vacsuit texture/wornGraphicPath outright
  (Things/Pawn/Humanlike/Apparel/Vacsuit/Vacsuit) with a warm tint —
  legitimate shipped DLC art for exactly this kind of garment, not a
  placeholder standing in for a mismatched subject. infrastructure/artpipe/
  {done,pending}/registry.jsonl carries nothing for "suit"/"heated"/"vacuum"
  this session (checked before writing this file) — nothing to reuse from
  our own pipeline, and nothing further queued: this art already fits.

  🔴 CORRECTED 2026-09-28 (THEY_MOD_REPLICATION_1 live-verify pass, unrelated
  item — fixed on sight per CLAUDE.md "correctness outranks seat ownership"):
  ParentName="Apparel_Vacsuit" NEVER resolved. RimWorld's XmlInheritance
  (Verse/XmlInheritance.cs, GetBestParentFor) indexes parent candidates ONLY
  by an XML node's own `Name="..."` attribute — never by <defName>. Vanilla's
  own Apparel_Vacsuit ThingDef (Data/Odyssey/Defs/ThingDefs_Misc/
  Apparel_Various.xml) carries no Name= attribute (it is a concrete,
  playable def, not an inheritance template), so this pattern silently
  produced "XML error: Could not find parent node named Apparel_Vacsuit" on
  EVERY load, leaving thingClass null — which then NREs
  ReadingPolicyDatabase.GenerateStartingPolicies() (item.thingClass.
  SameOrSubclassOf<Book>() on a null thingClass) inside Game..ctor(),
  crashing new-colony creation, quicktest AND campaign save load alike, the
  moment this def is active. Root-caused live via RimSage against the
  decompiled engine before touching anything. Fixed by inheriting from the
  actual abstract template (ParentName="ApparelBase", which DOES carry
  Name="ApparelBase") and restating, verbatim, the fields Apparel_Vacsuit
  itself adds on top of that base — this def now states everything the
  original header claimed was "inherited for free", because none of it
  actually was.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="ApparelBase" MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">
    <defName>RM_ChillHeatedSuit</defName>
    <label>heated dive suit</label>
    <description>A vacuum-rated suit rebuilt around a battery-fed heating web instead of a passive shell — it recycles the wearer's air same as any vacsuit, but the real work is the coils. On the Chill's seabed the ambient cold alone would kill in hours; this is the only thing standing between a working pawn and that. The gauge on its own wrist display is not a fuel light. When it reads empty, the suit is just a heavy coat, and the cold does not wait.</description>
    <generateAllowChance>0</generateAllowChance>
    <techLevel>Spacer</techLevel>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Pawn/Humanlike/Apparel/Vacsuit/Vacsuit</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
      <drawSize>0.9</drawSize>
      <color>(214, 108, 48)</color>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <!-- Copied verbatim from Apparel_Vacsuit (see 2026-09-28 header note —
           ParentName inheritance from it never actually worked), except
           Insulation_Cold, cut from 90 to 20: the real -110C protection is
           100% charge-gated, see file header and the .cs header. -->
      <WorkToMake>48000</WorkToMake>
      <MaxHitPoints>180</MaxHitPoints>
      <Mass>12</Mass>
      <Flammability>0.4</Flammability>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>0.52</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>0.25</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <ArmorRating_Heat>0.66</ArmorRating_Heat>
      <Insulation_Cold>20</Insulation_Cold>
      <Insulation_Heat>15</Insulation_Heat>
      <EquipDelay>14</EquipDelay>
    </statBases>
    <equippedStatOffsets>
      <MoveSpeed>-1.25</MoveSpeed>
      <VacuumResistance>0.32</VacuumResistance>
    </equippedStatOffsets>
    <thingCategories>
      <li>ApparelArmor</li>
    </thingCategories>
    <tradeTags>
      <li>HiTechArmor</li>
      <li>Armor</li>
    </tradeTags>
    <smeltable>true</smeltable>
    <apparel>
      <bodyPartGroups>
        <li>Torso</li>
        <li>Neck</li>
        <li>Shoulders</li>
        <li>Arms</li>
        <li>Legs</li>
      </bodyPartGroups>
      <wornGraphicPath>Things/Pawn/Humanlike/Apparel/Vacsuit/Vacsuit</wornGraphicPath>
      <layers>
        <li>Middle</li>
        <li>Shell</li>
      </layers>
      <tags>
        <li>SpacerMilitary</li>
        <li>Vacsuit</li>
      </tags>
      <defaultOutfitTags>
        <li>Spacefarer</li>
      </defaultOutfitTags>
      <useDeflectMetalEffect>true</useDeflectMetalEffect>
      <soundWear>Wear_PowerArmor</soundWear>
      <soundRemove>Remove_PowerArmor</soundRemove>
    </apparel>
    <costList>
      <ComponentIndustrial>3</ComponentIndustrial>
      <Steel>90</Steel>
      <Plasteel>20</Plasteel>
    </costList>
    <recipeMaker>
      <researchPrerequisite>OrbitalTech</researchPrerequisite>
      <unfinishedThingDef>UnfinishedTechArmor</unfinishedThingDef>
      <displayPriority>235</displayPriority>
      <workSpeedStat>GeneralLaborSpeed</workSpeedStat>
      <workSkill>Crafting</workSkill>
      <effectWorking>Smith</effectWorking>
      <soundWorking>Recipe_Smith</soundWorking>
      <recipeUsers>
        <li>TableMachining</li>
      </recipeUsers>
    </recipeMaker>
    <comps>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.DivingInteraction.RM_CompProperties_HeatedSuitBattery">
        <maxChargeTicks>15000</maxChargeTicks>
        <drainIntervalTicks>250</drainIntervalTicks>
        <rechargeRateMultiplier>3</rechargeRateMultiplier>
        <chargerSearchRadius>3.9</chargerSearchRadius>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
